      "knowledge_point": "Differentiating a Negative Power Function Using the Constant Multiple Rule",
      "problem": "If $y=-\\frac{3}{{x}^{7}},$ find $\\frac{dy}{dx}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We first rewrite the function as\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{3}{{x}^{7}}=-3{x}^{-7}.\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the constant multiple and power rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3{x}^{-7}) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{-7}) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot (-7){x}^{-7-1} \\\\  & =21{x}^{-8} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{{x}^{8}}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
