      "problem": "Which angle is coterminal with $-{175}^{\u2218}?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $ (in degrees), we add and subtract integer multiples of ${360}^{\u2218}$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of ${360}^{\u2218}$ to $-{175}^{\u2218}$:\n\n- $-{175}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}={185}^{\u2218}$\n\n- $-{175}^{\u2218}+2\\cdot {360}^{\u2218}={545}^{\u2218}\\,\u2713$\n\nThere are no answer choices larger than ${545}^{\u2218},$ so we can stop here.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of ${360}^{\u2218}$ from $-{175}^{\u2218}$:\n\n- $-{175}^{\u2218}-{360}^{\u2218}=-{535}^{\u2218}$\n\n- $-{175}^{\u2218}-2\\cdot {360}^{\u2218}=-{895}^{\u2218}$\n\nThere are no answer choices smaller than $-{895}^{\u2218},$ so we can stop here.\n\nSo the correct answer is ${545}^{\u2218}.$",
